    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187A(4) Service providers must keep certain information and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187a-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(4) This section does not require a service provider to keep, or cause to\nbe kept:\n\n(a) information that is the contents or substance of a\ncommunication; or\nNote:\nThis paragraph puts beyond doubt that service providers are not\nrequired to keep information about telecommunications content.\n\n(b) information that:\n\n(i) states an address to which a communication was sent on\nthe internet, from a telecommunications device, using\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 1  Data retention",
      "skos:definition": "(4) This section does not require a service provider to keep, or cause to\nbe kept:\n\n(a) information that is the contents or substance of a\ncommunication; or\nNote:\nThis paragraph puts beyond doubt that service providers are not\nrequired to keep information about telecommunications content.\n\n(b) information that:\n\n(i) states an address to which a communication was sent on\nthe internet, from a telecommunications device, using\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 1  Data retention",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "08ad15588978f93456b5fa12273e89f2249db789b6b1590aa90fdf2f1b43e688",
      "skos:note": "Service providers must keep certain information",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187A(4) Service providers must keep certain information and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(4) This section does not require a service provider to keep, or cause to\nbe kept:\n\n(a) information that is the contents or substance of a\ncommunication; or\nNote:\nThis paragraph puts beyond doubt that service providers are not\nrequired to keep information about telecommunications content.\n\n(b) information that:\n\n(i) states an address to which a communication was sent on\nthe internet, from a telecommunications device, using\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 1  Data retention"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187a-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
