    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187C Period for keeping information and documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The period for which a service provider must keep, or cause to be\nkept, information or a document under section 187A is:\n\n(a) if the information is about, or the document contains\ninformation about, a matter of a kind described in\nparagraph (a) or (b) in column 2 of item 1 of the table in\nsubsection 187AA(1)—the period:\n\n(i) starting when the information or document came into\nexistence; and\n\n(ii) ending 2 years after the closure of the account to which\nthe information or document relates; or\n\n(b) otherwise—the period:\n\n(i) starting when the information or document came into\nexistence; and\n\n(ii) ending 2 years after it came into existence.\n\n(2) However, the regulations may prescribe that, in relation to a\nspecified matter of a kind described in paragraph (a) or (b) in\ncolumn 2 of item 1 of the table in subsection 187AA(1), the period\nunder subsection (1) of this section is the period referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b) of this section.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 1  Data retention",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The period for which a service provider must keep, or cause to be\nkept, information or a document under section 187A is:\n\n(a) if the information is about, or the document contains\ninformation about, a matter of a kind described in\nparagraph (a) or (b) in column 2 of item 1 of the table in\nsubsection 187AA(1)—the period:\n\n(i) starting when the information or document came into\nexistence; and\n\n(ii) ending 2 years after the closure of the account to which\nthe information or document relates; or\n\n(b) otherwise—the period:\n\n(i) starting when the information or document came into\nexistence; and\n\n(ii) ending 2 years after it came into existence.\n\n(2) However, the regulations may prescribe that, in relation to a\nspecified matter of a kind described in paragraph (a) or (b) in\ncolumn 2 of item 1 of the table in subsection 187AA(1), the period\nunder subsection (1) of this section is the period referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b) of this section.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 1  Data retention",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3372df20f76c8e7ef101bee1e3f9994b17ff0d78c16603e324a0329c0bef70ef"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187C Period for keeping information and documents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The period for which a service provider must keep, or cause to be\nkept, information or a document under section 187A is:\n\n(a) if the information is about, or the document contains\ninformation about, a matter of a kind described in\nparagraph (a) or (b) in column 2 of item 1 of the table in\nsubsection 187AA(1)—the period:\n\n(i) starting when the information or document came into\nexistence; and\n\n(ii) ending 2 years after the closure of the account to which\nthe information or document relates; or\n\n(b) otherwise—the period:\n\n(i) starting when the information or document came into\nexistence; and\n\n(ii) ending 2 years after it came into existence.\n\n(2) However, the regulations may prescribe that, in relation to a\nspecified matter of a kind described in paragraph (a) or (b) in\ncolumn 2 of item 1 of the table in subsection 187AA(1), the period\nunder subsection (1) of this section is the period referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b) of this section.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 1  Data retention"
    },
