          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187e-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187e-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f909971b7988c1e934dbceca3b04fa910d566f6b2a9674d28ea74b6f8dd1c1c3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187E Applying for approval of data retention implementation plans",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A service provider may apply to the Communications Access\nCo-ordinator for approval of a data retention implementation plan\nfor one or more relevant services operated by the service provider.\n\n(2) The plan must specify, in relation to each such service:\n\n(a) an explanation of the current practices for keeping, and\nensuring the confidentiality of, information and documents\nthat section 187A would require to be kept, if the plan were\nnot in force; and\n\n(b) details of the interim arrangements that the service provider\nproposes to be implemented, while the plan is in force, for\nkeeping, and ensuring the confidentiality of, such information\nand documents (to the extent that the information and\ndocuments will not be kept in compliance with section 187A\n(and sections 187BA and 187C)); and\n\n(c) the day by which the service provider will comply with\nsection 187A (and sections 187BA and 187C) in relation to\nall such information and documents, except to the extent that\nany decisions under Division 3 apply.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\n(3) The day specified under paragraph (2)(c) must not be later than the\nday on which the plan would, if approved, cease to be in force\nunder section 187H in relation to the service.\n\n(4) The plan must also specify:\n\n(a) any relevant services, operated by the service provider, that\nthe plan does not cover; and\n\n(b) the contact details of the officers or employees of the service\nprovider in relation to the plan."
    },
