    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187g-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187G(3) Consultation with agencies and the ACMA",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The service provider must respond to a request for an amendment\nof the original plan either:\n\n(a) by indicating its acceptance of the request, by amending the\noriginal plan appropriately and by giving the amended plan to\nthe Communications Access Co-ordinator within the\nresponse period; or\n\n(b) by indicating that it does not accept the request and providing\nits reasons for that non-acceptance.\nThe ACMA’s role"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187g-ss-3-norm",
