    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187g-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187G(5) Consultation with agencies and the ACMA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187g-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The ACMA must then:\n\n(a) determine in writing that no amendment of the original plan\nis required in response to the request for the amendment; or\n\n(b) if, in the opinion of the ACMA:\n\n(i) the request for the amendment is a reasonable one; and\n\n(ii) the service provider’s response to the request for the\namendment is not reasonable;\n\ndetermine in writing that the original plan should be amended\nin a specified manner and give a copy of the determination to\nthe service provider.\nCo-ordinator to approve amended plan or to refuse approval",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The ACMA must then:\n\n(a) determine in writing that no amendment of the original plan\nis required in response to the request for the amendment; or\n\n(b) if, in the opinion of the ACMA:\n\n(i) the request for the amendment is a reasonable one; and\n\n(ii) the service provider’s response to the request for the\namendment is not reasonable;\n\ndetermine in writing that the original plan should be amended\nin a specified manner and give a copy of the determination to\nthe service provider.\nCo-ordinator to approve amended plan or to refuse approval",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187g"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187g-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187g-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5edd034bda3b29e7518b75fbbeb47c72ec6fa84869f82239848547b9154d7809",
      "skos:note": "Determine in writing that the original plan should be amended in a specified manner and give a copy of the determination to the service provider.",
      "dc:description": "Copy of determination"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187g-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187G(5) Consultation with agencies and the ACMA",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The ACMA must then:\n\n(a) determine in writing that no amendment of the original plan\nis required in response to the request for the amendment; or\n\n(b) if, in the opinion of the ACMA:\n\n(i) the request for the amendment is a reasonable one; and\n\n(ii) the service provider’s response to the request for the\namendment is not reasonable;\n\ndetermine in writing that the original plan should be amended\nin a specified manner and give a copy of the determination to\nthe service provider.\nCo-ordinator to approve amended plan or to refuse approval"
    },
