    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187J Amending data retention implementation plans",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a service provider’s data retention implementation plan is in\nforce, it may be amended only if:\n\n(a) the service provider applies to the Communications Access\nCo-ordinator for approval of the amendment, and the\nCo-ordinator approves the amendment; or\n\n(b) the Co-ordinator makes a request to the service provider for\nthe amendment to be made, and the service provider agrees to\nthe amendment.\n\n(2) Section 187F applies in relation to approval of the amendment\nunder paragraph (1)(a) as if the application for approval of the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\namendment were an application under section 187E for approval of\na data retention implementation plan.\n\n(3) An amendment of a data retention implementation plan:\n\n(a) comes into force when:\n\n(i) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—the Co-ordinator notifies\nthe service provider of the approval of the amendment;\nor\n\n(ii) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the service provider\nnotifies the Co-ordinator of the service provider’s\nagreement to the amendment; but\n\n(b) does not effect when the plan ceases to be in force under\nparagraph 187H(1)(b).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a service provider’s data retention implementation plan is in\nforce, it may be amended only if:\n\n(a) the service provider applies to the Communications Access\nCo-ordinator for approval of the amendment, and the\nCo-ordinator approves the amendment; or\n\n(b) the Co-ordinator makes a request to the service provider for\nthe amendment to be made, and the service provider agrees to\nthe amendment.\n\n(2) Section 187F applies in relation to approval of the amendment\nunder paragraph (1)(a) as if the application for approval of the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\namendment were an application under section 187E for approval of\na data retention implementation plan.\n\n(3) An amendment of a data retention implementation plan:\n\n(a) comes into force when:\n\n(i) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—the Co-ordinator notifies\nthe service provider of the approval of the amendment;\nor\n\n(ii) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the service provider\nnotifies the Co-ordinator of the service provider’s\nagreement to the amendment; but\n\n(b) does not effect when the plan ceases to be in force under\nparagraph 187H(1)(b).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187j-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e4e9526d32a40fcbba9f1e21dce65a4a1f01f171dfeac2f0c3df6f0bf95e4ce9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187J Amending data retention implementation plans",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a service provider’s data retention implementation plan is in\nforce, it may be amended only if:\n\n(a) the service provider applies to the Communications Access\nCo-ordinator for approval of the amendment, and the\nCo-ordinator approves the amendment; or\n\n(b) the Co-ordinator makes a request to the service provider for\nthe amendment to be made, and the service provider agrees to\nthe amendment.\n\n(2) Section 187F applies in relation to approval of the amendment\nunder paragraph (1)(a) as if the application for approval of the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\namendment were an application under section 187E for approval of\na data retention implementation plan.\n\n(3) An amendment of a data retention implementation plan:\n\n(a) comes into force when:\n\n(i) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—the Co-ordinator notifies\nthe service provider of the approval of the amendment;\nor\n\n(ii) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the service provider\nnotifies the Co-ordinator of the service provider’s\nagreement to the amendment; but\n\n(b) does not effect when the plan ceases to be in force under\nparagraph 187H(1)(b)."
    },
    {
