    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187K The Communications Access Co-ordinator may grant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "exemptions or variations\nDecision to exempt or vary\n\n(1) The Communications Access Co-ordinator may:\n\n(a) exempt a specified service provider from the obligations\nimposed on the service provider under this Part, either\ngenerally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of\nrelevant service; or\n\n(b) vary the obligations imposed on a specified service provider\nunder this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a\nspecified kind of relevant service; or\n\n(c) vary, in relation to a specified service provider, a period\nspecified in section 187C, either generally or in relation to\ninformation or documents that relate to a specified kind of\nrelevant service.\nA variation must not impose obligations that would exceed the\nobligations to which a service provider would otherwise be subject\nunder sections 187A and 187C.\n\n(2) The decision must be in writing.\n\n(3) The decision may be:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 1  Data retention",
      "skos:definition": "exemptions or variations\nDecision to exempt or vary\n\n(1) The Communications Access Co-ordinator may:\n\n(a) exempt a specified service provider from the obligations\nimposed on the service provider under this Part, either\ngenerally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of\nrelevant service; or\n\n(b) vary the obligations imposed on a specified service provider\nunder this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a\nspecified kind of relevant service; or\n\n(c) vary, in relation to a specified service provider, a period\nspecified in section 187C, either generally or in relation to\ninformation or documents that relate to a specified kind of\nrelevant service.\nA variation must not impose obligations that would exceed the\nobligations to which a service provider would otherwise be subject\nunder sections 187A and 187C.\n\n(2) The decision must be in writing.\n\n(3) The decision may be:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 1  Data retention",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187k-ss-1"
        },
