    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187L Confidentiality of applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Communications Access Co-ordinator receives a service\nprovider’s application under section 187E for approval of a data\nretention implementation plan, or application for a decision under\nsubsection 187K(1), the Co-ordinator must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than the ACMA, an enforcement agency or a security\nauthority) without the written permission of the service\nprovider.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\n(1A) If the ACMA receives a service provider’s application under\nsection 187KA for review of a decision under subsection 187K(1),\nthe ACMA must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority) without the\nwritten permission of the service provider.\n\n(2) The ACMA, the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority must, if it receives\nunder subsection 187G(1), paragraph 187K(5)(a) or\nsubsection 187KA(3) a copy of a service provider’s application:\n\n(a) treat the copy as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\nwithout the written permission of the service provider.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Communications Access Co-ordinator receives a service\nprovider’s application under section 187E for approval of a data\nretention implementation plan, or application for a decision under\nsubsection 187K(1), the Co-ordinator must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than the ACMA, an enforcement agency or a security\nauthority) without the written permission of the service\nprovider.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\n(1A) If the ACMA receives a service provider’s application under\nsection 187KA for review of a decision under subsection 187K(1),\nthe ACMA must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority) without the\nwritten permission of the service provider.\n\n(2) The ACMA, the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority must, if it receives\nunder subsection 187G(1), paragraph 187K(5)(a) or\nsubsection 187KA(3) a copy of a service provider’s application:\n\n(a) treat the copy as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\nwithout the written permission of the service provider.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bfeb80c190c7020feb0225debadafdacac925a4fe10b9281e0b13af73e6b7c00"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187L Confidentiality of applications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Communications Access Co-ordinator receives a service\nprovider’s application under section 187E for approval of a data\nretention implementation plan, or application for a decision under\nsubsection 187K(1), the Co-ordinator must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than the ACMA, an enforcement agency or a security\nauthority) without the written permission of the service\nprovider.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\n(1A) If the ACMA receives a service provider’s application under\nsection 187KA for review of a decision under subsection 187K(1),\nthe ACMA must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority) without the\nwritten permission of the service provider.\n\n(2) The ACMA, the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority must, if it receives\nunder subsection 187G(1), paragraph 187K(5)(a) or\nsubsection 187KA(3) a copy of a service provider’s application:\n\n(a) treat the copy as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\nwithout the written permission of the service provider."
    },
    {
