    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187L(1A) Confidentiality of applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187l-ss-1a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) If the ACMA receives a service provider’s application under\nsection 187KA for review of a decision under subsection 187K(1),\nthe ACMA must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority) without the\nwritten permission of the service provider.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) If the ACMA receives a service provider’s application under\nsection 187KA for review of a decision under subsection 187K(1),\nthe ACMA must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority) without the\nwritten permission of the service provider.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
