    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187L(2) Confidentiality of applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187l-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The ACMA, the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority must, if it receives\nunder subsection 187G(1), paragraph 187K(5)(a) or\nsubsection 187KA(3) a copy of a service provider’s application:\n\n(a) treat the copy as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\nwithout the written permission of the service provider.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The ACMA, the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority must, if it receives\nunder subsection 187G(1), paragraph 187K(5)(a) or\nsubsection 187KA(3) a copy of a service provider’s application:\n\n(a) treat the copy as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\nwithout the written permission of the service provider.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a9e70b71b0f41ccabeb912ca4551183239cc36d5c022e6905d77d90ecb65b6d8",
      "skos:note": "Must treat copy of application as confidential and ensure it is not disclosed without permission."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-187l-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187L(2) Confidentiality of applications",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The ACMA, the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority must, if it receives\nunder subsection 187G(1), paragraph 187K(5)(a) or\nsubsection 187KA(3) a copy of a service provider’s application:\n\n(a) treat the copy as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\nwithout the written permission of the service provider."
    },
