      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(2B) A report under subsection (1) is to set out the matters referred to in\nparagraph (2A)(e) by specifying:\n\n(a) in relation to each of 8 successive periods of 3 months, the\nnumber of the authorisations sought for information or\ndocuments held for lengths of time included in that period;\nand\n\n(b) the number of the authorisations sought for information or\ndocuments held for lengths of time exceeding 24 months.\n\n(2C) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare kinds of\ninformation that are to be set out in a report under subsection (1).\nIntelligence Services Act 2001",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(2B) A report under subsection (1) is to set out the matters referred to in\nparagraph (2A)(e) by specifying:\n\n(a) in relation to each of 8 successive periods of 3 months, the\nnumber of the authorisations sought for information or\ndocuments held for lengths of time included in that period;\nand\n\n(b) the number of the authorisations sought for information or\ndocuments held for lengths of time exceeding 24 months.\n\n(2C) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare kinds of\ninformation that are to be set out in a report under subsection (1).\nIntelligence Services Act 2001",
      "cml:hasPart": [
