    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-1g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1G At the end of section 29",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-1g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(4) Subject to subsection (5), paragraphs (3)(c) and (k) do not apply to\nthings done in the performance of the Committee’s functions under\nparagraphs (1)(bd) and (be).\n\n(5) The Committee’s functions under paragraphs (1)(bd) and (be):\n\n(a) are to be performed for the sole purpose of assessing, and\nmaking recommendations on, the overall operation and\neffectiveness of Part 5-1A of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979; and\n\n(b) do not permit reviewing the retained data activities of service\nproviders; and\n\n(c) may not be performed for any purpose other than that set out\nin paragraph (a).\nNote:\nThe performance of the Committee’s functions under\nparagraphs (1)(bd) and (be) are also subject to the requirements of\nSchedule 1.\nPrivacy Act 1988",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(4) Subject to subsection (5), paragraphs (3)(c) and (k) do not apply to\nthings done in the performance of the Committee’s functions under\nparagraphs (1)(bd) and (be).\n\n(5) The Committee’s functions under paragraphs (1)(bd) and (be):\n\n(a) are to be performed for the sole purpose of assessing, and\nmaking recommendations on, the overall operation and\neffectiveness of Part 5-1A of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979; and\n\n(b) do not permit reviewing the retained data activities of service\nproviders; and\n\n(c) may not be performed for any purpose other than that set out\nin paragraph (a).\nNote:\nThe performance of the Committee’s functions under\nparagraphs (1)(bd) and (be) are also subject to the requirements of\nSchedule 1.\nPrivacy Act 1988",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-1g-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-1g-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-1g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1G At the end of section 29",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(4) Subject to subsection (5), paragraphs (3)(c) and (k) do not apply to\nthings done in the performance of the Committee’s functions under\nparagraphs (1)(bd) and (be).\n\n(5) The Committee’s functions under paragraphs (1)(bd) and (be):\n\n(a) are to be performed for the sole purpose of assessing, and\nmaking recommendations on, the overall operation and\neffectiveness of Part 5-1A of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979; and\n\n(b) do not permit reviewing the retained data activities of service\nproviders; and\n\n(c) may not be performed for any purpose other than that set out\nin paragraph (a).\nNote:\nThe performance of the Committee’s functions under\nparagraphs (1)(bd) and (be) are also subject to the requirements of\nSchedule 1.\nPrivacy Act 1988"
    },
