    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3C At the end of section 281",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-3c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), this section does not apply to a disclosure\nof information or a document by a person as a witness in a civil\nproceeding if the information or document:\n\n(a) is kept, by a service provider (within the meaning of the\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979),\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\nsolely for the purpose of complying with Part 5-1A of that\nAct; and\n\n(b) is not used or disclosed by the service provider for any\npurpose other than one or more of the following purposes:\n\n(i) complying with Part 5-1A of that Act;\n\n(ii) complying with the requirements of warrants under\nChapters 2 and 3 of that Act or authorisations under\nChapter 4 of that Act;\n\n(iii) complying with requests or requirements to make\ndisclosures provided for by sections 284 to 288 of this\nAct;\n\n(iv) providing persons with access to their personal\ninformation in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988;\n\n(v) a purpose prescribed by the regulations;\n\n(vi) a purpose incidental to any of the purposes referred to in\nsubparagraphs (i) to (v).\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply:\n\n(a) in circumstances of a kind prescribed by the regulations; or\n\n(b) to a disclosure to an enforcement agency (within the meaning\nof the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979); or\n\n(c) to a disclosure that occurs during the implementation phase\n(within the meaning of that Act).",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), this section does not apply to a disclosure\nof information or a document by a person as a witness in a civil\nproceeding if the information or document:\n\n(a) is kept, by a service provider (within the meaning of the\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979),\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\nsolely for the purpose of complying with Part 5-1A of that\nAct; and\n\n(b) is not used or disclosed by the service provider for any\npurpose other than one or more of the following purposes:\n\n(i) complying with Part 5-1A of that Act;\n\n(ii) complying with the requirements of warrants under\nChapters 2 and 3 of that Act or authorisations under\nChapter 4 of that Act;\n\n(iii) complying with requests or requirements to make\ndisclosures provided for by sections 284 to 288 of this\nAct;\n\n(iv) providing persons with access to their personal\ninformation in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988;\n\n(v) a purpose prescribed by the regulations;\n\n(vi) a purpose incidental to any of the purposes referred to in\nsubparagraphs (i) to (v).\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply:\n\n(a) in circumstances of a kind prescribed by the regulations; or\n\n(b) to a disclosure to an enforcement agency (within the meaning\nof the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979); or\n\n(c) to a disclosure that occurs during the implementation phase\n(within the meaning of that Act).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-3c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3C At the end of section 281",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), this section does not apply to a disclosure\nof information or a document by a person as a witness in a civil\nproceeding if the information or document:\n\n(a) is kept, by a service provider (within the meaning of the\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979),\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\nsolely for the purpose of complying with Part 5-1A of that\nAct; and\n\n(b) is not used or disclosed by the service provider for any\npurpose other than one or more of the following purposes:\n\n(i) complying with Part 5-1A of that Act;\n\n(ii) complying with the requirements of warrants under\nChapters 2 and 3 of that Act or authorisations under\nChapter 4 of that Act;\n\n(iii) complying with requests or requirements to make\ndisclosures provided for by sections 284 to 288 of this\nAct;\n\n(iv) providing persons with access to their personal\ninformation in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988;\n\n(v) a purpose prescribed by the regulations;\n\n(vi) a purpose incidental to any of the purposes referred to in\nsubparagraphs (i) to (v).\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply:\n\n(a) in circumstances of a kind prescribed by the regulations; or\n\n(b) to a disclosure to an enforcement agency (within the meaning\nof the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979); or\n\n(c) to a disclosure that occurs during the implementation phase\n(within the meaning of that Act)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3c-ss-2",
