    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180l-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180L(2) Issuing a journalist information warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-180l-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Minister must not issue a journalist information warrant unless\nthe Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the Organisation’s functions would extend to the making of\nauthorisations under Division 3 in relation to the particular\nperson; and\n\n(b) the public interest in issuing the warrant outweighs the public\ninterest in protecting the confidentiality of the identity of the\nsource in connection with whom authorisations would be\nmade under the authority of the warrant, having regard to:\n\n(i) the extent to which the privacy of any person or persons\nwould be likely to be interfered with by the disclosure\nof information or documents under authorisations that\nare likely to be made under the authority of the warrant;\nand\n\n(ii) the gravity of the matter in relation to which the warrant\nis sought; and\n\n(iii) the extent to which that information or those documents\nwould be likely to assist in the performance of the\nOrganisation’s functions; and\n\n(iv) whether reasonable attempts have been made to obtain\nthe information or documents by other means; and\n\n(v) any submissions made by a Public Interest Advocate\nunder section 180X; and\n\n(vi) any other matters the Minister considers relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Minister must not issue a journalist information warrant unless\nthe Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the Organisation’s functions would extend to the making of\nauthorisations under Division 3 in relation to the particular\nperson; and\n\n(b) the public interest in issuing the warrant outweighs the public\ninterest in protecting the confidentiality of the identity of the\nsource in connection with whom authorisations would be\nmade under the authority of the warrant, having regard to:\n\n(i) the extent to which the privacy of any person or persons\nwould be likely to be interfered with by the disclosure\nof information or documents under authorisations that\nare likely to be made under the authority of the warrant;\nand\n\n(ii) the gravity of the matter in relation to which the warrant\nis sought; and\n\n(iii) the extent to which that information or those documents\nwould be likely to assist in the performance of the\nOrganisation’s functions; and\n\n(iv) whether reasonable attempts have been made to obtain\nthe information or documents by other means; and\n\n(v) any submissions made by a Public Interest Advocate\nunder section 180X; and\n\n(vi) any other matters the Minister considers relevant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180l"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180l-ss-2-norm"
        },
