      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180P Discontinuance of authorisations before expiry of a journalist",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-180p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "information warrant\n\nIf, before a journalist information warrant issued under this\nSubdivision ceases to be in force, the Director-General of Security\nis satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have\nceased to exist, he or she must:\n\n(a) forthwith inform the Minister accordingly; and\n\n(b) takes such steps as are necessary to ensure that the making of\nauthorisations under the authority of the warrant is\ndiscontinued.\nSubdivision C—Issuing journalist information warrants to\nenforcement agencies",
      "skos:definition": "information warrant\n\nIf, before a journalist information warrant issued under this\nSubdivision ceases to be in force, the Director-General of Security\nis satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have\nceased to exist, he or she must:\n\n(a) forthwith inform the Minister accordingly; and\n\n(b) takes such steps as are necessary to ensure that the making of\nauthorisations under the authority of the warrant is\ndiscontinued.\nSubdivision C—Issuing journalist information warrants to\nenforcement agencies",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180p-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180p-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f54f27d1dff2fee34108d1c0ff3a46cab8421e96be33552ac6b6fbfc40dd0ee0",
      "skos:note": "Ensure discontinuation of authorisations before expiry of a journalist information warrant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-180p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180P Discontinuance of authorisations before expiry of a journalist",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "information warrant\n\nIf, before a journalist information warrant issued under this\nSubdivision ceases to be in force, the Director-General of Security\nis satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have\nceased to exist, he or she must:\n\n(a) forthwith inform the Minister accordingly; and\n\n(b) takes such steps as are necessary to ensure that the making of\nauthorisations under the authority of the warrant is\ndiscontinued.\nSubdivision C—Issuing journalist information warrants to\nenforcement agencies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180p-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180p"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180p-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to inform the Minister and take steps to ensure discontinuation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180Q Enforcement agency may apply for a journalist information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-180q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "warrant\n\n(1) An enforcement agency may apply to a Part 4-1 issuing authority\nfor a journalist information warrant in relation to a particular\nperson.\n\n(2) The application must be made on the agency’s behalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subsection 39(2)—a person\nreferred to in that subsection in relation to that agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The chief officer of the agency may, in writing, nominate for the\npurposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) an office or position in the\nagency that is involved in the management of the agency.\n\n(4) A nomination under subsection (3) is not a legislative instrument.\n\n(5) The application may be made in writing or in any other form.\nNote:\nThe Electronic Transactions Act 1999 deals with giving information\nin writing by means of an electronic communication.",
      "skos:definition": "warrant\n\n(1) An enforcement agency may apply to a Part 4-1 issuing authority\nfor a journalist information warrant in relation to a particular\nperson.\n\n(2) The application must be made on the agency’s behalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subsection 39(2)—a person\nreferred to in that subsection in relation to that agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The chief officer of the agency may, in writing, nominate for the\npurposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) an office or position in the\nagency that is involved in the management of the agency.\n\n(4) A nomination under subsection (3) is not a legislative instrument.\n\n(5) The application may be made in writing or in any other form.\nNote:\nThe Electronic Transactions Act 1999 deals with giving information\nin writing by means of an electronic communication.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180q-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180q-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180q-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-180q-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d9bceb39819ed7a46968c3f9b31b50cfcf09492d3472ea264640caad3d3609c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-180q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180Q Enforcement agency may apply for a journalist information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "warrant\n\n(1) An enforcement agency may apply to a Part 4-1 issuing authority\nfor a journalist information warrant in relation to a particular\nperson.\n\n(2) The application must be made on the agency’s behalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subsection 39(2)—a person\nreferred to in that subsection in relation to that agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nData retention  Schedule 1\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The chief officer of the agency may, in writing, nominate for the\npurposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) an office or position in the\nagency that is involved in the management of the agency.\n\n(4) A nomination under subsection (3) is not a legislative instrument.\n\n(5) The application may be made in writing or in any other form.\nNote:\nThe Electronic Transactions Act 1999 deals with giving information\nin writing by means of an electronic communication."
    },
