    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-6t",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6T Subsection 182(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-6t"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nExempt disclosures\n\n(2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a disclosure of non-missing\nperson information if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is reasonably necessary:\n\n(i) for a person to comply with his or her obligations under\nsection 185D or 185E; or\n\n(ii) for the performance by the Organisation of its functions;\nor\n\n(iii) for the enforcement of the criminal law; or\n\n(iv) for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary\npenalty; or\n\n(v) for the protection of the public revenue; or\n\n(b) the disclosure is:\n\n(i) to an IGIS official for the purpose of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nexercising powers, or performing functions or duties,\nunder the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nAct 1986; or\n\n(ii) by an IGIS official in connection with the IGIS official\nexercising powers, or performing functions or duties,\nunder that Act.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nExempt disclosures\n\n(2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a disclosure of non-missing\nperson information if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is reasonably necessary:\n\n(i) for a person to comply with his or her obligations under\nsection 185D or 185E; or\n\n(ii) for the performance by the Organisation of its functions;\nor\n\n(iii) for the enforcement of the criminal law; or\n\n(iv) for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary\npenalty; or\n\n(v) for the protection of the public revenue; or\n\n(b) the disclosure is:\n\n(i) to an IGIS official for the purpose of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nexercising powers, or performing functions or duties,\nunder the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nAct 1986; or\n\n(ii) by an IGIS official in connection with the IGIS official\nexercising powers, or performing functions or duties,\nunder that Act.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-6t-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-6t-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a44e02007e00094d12d9a22a88227d60115423fc269adc9558320905d7b5acd1",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of non-missing person information is permitted under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-1-sec-6t",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6T Subsection 182(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nExempt disclosures\n\n(2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a disclosure of non-missing\nperson information if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is reasonably necessary:\n\n(i) for a person to comply with his or her obligations under\nsection 185D or 185E; or\n\n(ii) for the performance by the Organisation of its functions;\nor\n\n(iii) for the enforcement of the criminal law; or\n\n(iv) for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary\npenalty; or\n\n(v) for the protection of the public revenue; or\n\n(b) the disclosure is:\n\n(i) to an IGIS official for the purpose of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nexercising powers, or performing functions or duties,\nunder the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nAct 1986; or\n\n(ii) by an IGIS official in connection with the IGIS official\nexercising powers, or performing functions or duties,\nunder that Act.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."
    },
