    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-110a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "110A Meaning of criminal law-enforcement agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-2-sec-110a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.61",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each of the following is a criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(b) a Police Force of a State;\n\n(c) the Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity;\n\n(d) the ACC;\n\n(e) the Australian Customs and Border Protection Service;\n\n(ea) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission;\n\n(eb) the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission;\n\n(f) the Crime Commission;\n\n(g) the Independent Commission Against Corruption;\n\n(h) the Police Integrity Commission;\n\n(i) the IBAC;\n\n(j) the Crime and Corruption Commission of Queensland;\n\n(k) the Corruption and Crime Commission;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 2  Restricting access to stored communications and telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Each of the following is a criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(b) a Police Force of a State;\n\n(c) the Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity;\n\n(d) the ACC;\n\n(e) the Australian Customs and Border Protection Service;\n\n(ea) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission;\n\n(eb) the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission;\n\n(f) the Crime Commission;\n\n(g) the Independent Commission Against Corruption;\n\n(h) the Police Integrity Commission;\n\n(i) the IBAC;\n\n(j) the Crime and Corruption Commission of Queensland;\n\n(k) the Corruption and Crime Commission;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 2  Restricting access to stored communications and telecommunications data",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-110a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-110a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ef47eb9c0f9aa839b04f387cec2c74d59e764dfd549d1ef49ffa44020a3251e7",
      "skos:note": "List of criminal law-enforcement agencies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-2-sec-110a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "110A Meaning of criminal law-enforcement agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 61,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each of the following is a criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(b) a Police Force of a State;\n\n(c) the Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity;\n\n(d) the ACC;\n\n(e) the Australian Customs and Border Protection Service;\n\n(ea) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission;\n\n(eb) the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission;\n\n(f) the Crime Commission;\n\n(g) the Independent Commission Against Corruption;\n\n(h) the Police Integrity Commission;\n\n(i) the IBAC;\n\n(j) the Crime and Corruption Commission of Queensland;\n\n(k) the Corruption and Crime Commission;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 2  Restricting access to stored communications and telecommunications data"
    },
    {
