      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3B) The Minister must not make the declaration unless...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the Minister is not satisfied on reasonable grounds that..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-176a-ss-3b-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "During",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Minister's satisfaction on reasonable grounds must occur during declaration-making process.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3B) The Minister must not make the declaration unless...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the Minister is satisfied on reasonable grounds that..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-176a-ss-3b-logic-ltl-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Minister's declaration only applies until functions of authority or body change.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3B) The Minister must not make the declaration unless...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the functions of the authority or body no longer include: (a) enforcement of the criminal law; or..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-176a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "176A(4) Meaning of enforcement agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-2-sec-176a-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In considering whether to make the declaration, the Minister must\nhave regard to:\n\n(b) whether the making of authorisations under section 178 or\n179 would be reasonably likely to assist the authority or body\nin performing the functions referred to in subsection (3B);\nand\n\n(c) whether the authority or body:\n\n(i) is required to comply with the Australian Privacy\nPrinciples; or\n\n(ii) is required to comply with a binding scheme that\nprovides protection of personal information that meets\nthe requirements of subsection (4A); or\n\n(iii) has agreed in writing to comply with a scheme\nproviding such protection of personal information, in\nrelation to personal information disclosed to it under\nChapter 4, if the declaration is made; and\n\n(d) whether the authority or body proposes to adopt processes\nand practices that would ensure its compliance with the\nobligations of an enforcement agency under Chapter 4; and\n\n(e) whether the Minister considers that the declaration would be\nin the public interest; and\n\n(f) any other matter that the Minister considers relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In considering whether to make the declaration, the Minister must\nhave regard to:\n\n(b) whether the making of authorisations under section 178 or\n179 would be reasonably likely to assist the authority or body\nin performing the functions referred to in subsection (3B);\nand\n\n(c) whether the authority or body:\n\n(i) is required to comply with the Australian Privacy\nPrinciples; or\n\n(ii) is required to comply with a binding scheme that\nprovides protection of personal information that meets\nthe requirements of subsection (4A); or\n\n(iii) has agreed in writing to comply with a scheme\nproviding such protection of personal information, in\nrelation to personal information disclosed to it under\nChapter 4, if the declaration is made; and\n\n(d) whether the authority or body proposes to adopt processes\nand practices that would ensure its compliance with the\nobligations of an enforcement agency under Chapter 4; and\n\n(e) whether the Minister considers that the declaration would be\nin the public interest; and\n\n(f) any other matter that the Minister considers relevant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-176a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-176a-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f868aa18bdc88073e56f008cf2510a1b66aa48bba9f59b382a28c717204804a4",
      "skos:note": "Consideration of factors before making declaration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-2-sec-176a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "176A(4) Meaning of enforcement agency",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In considering whether to make the declaration, the Minister must\nhave regard to:\n\n(b) whether the making of authorisations under section 178 or\n179 would be reasonably likely to assist the authority or body\nin performing the functions referred to in subsection (3B);\nand\n\n(c) whether the authority or body:\n\n(i) is required to comply with the Australian Privacy\nPrinciples; or\n\n(ii) is required to comply with a binding scheme that\nprovides protection of personal information that meets\nthe requirements of subsection (4A); or\n\n(iii) has agreed in writing to comply with a scheme\nproviding such protection of personal information, in\nrelation to personal information disclosed to it under\nChapter 4, if the declaration is made; and\n\n(d) whether the authority or body proposes to adopt processes\nand practices that would ensure its compliance with the\nobligations of an enforcement agency under Chapter 4; and\n\n(e) whether the Minister considers that the declaration would be\nin the public interest; and\n\n(f) any other matter that the Minister considers relevant."
    },
