    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-50",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50 Existing authorisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-2-sec-50"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "If:\n\n(a) an authority or body made an authorisation under Division 4\nof Part 4-1 of the Telecommunications (Interception and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nRestricting access to stored communications and telecommunications data  Schedule 2\nApplication provisions  Part 3\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\nAccess) Act 1979 before the commencement of this Schedule;\nand\n\n(b) the authorisation was in force immediately before that\ncommencement; and\n\n(c) on that commencement, the authority or body is not an\nenforcement agency;\nafter that commencement, the authorisation continues in force, and\nChapter 4 of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979 as amended by this Act continues to apply in relation to the\nauthorisation, as if the authority or body were an enforcement agency.",
      "skos:definition": "If:\n\n(a) an authority or body made an authorisation under Division 4\nof Part 4-1 of the Telecommunications (Interception and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nRestricting access to stored communications and telecommunications data  Schedule 2\nApplication provisions  Part 3\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\nAccess) Act 1979 before the commencement of this Schedule;\nand\n\n(b) the authorisation was in force immediately before that\ncommencement; and\n\n(c) on that commencement, the authority or body is not an\nenforcement agency;\nafter that commencement, the authorisation continues in force, and\nChapter 4 of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979 as amended by this Act continues to apply in relation to the\nauthorisation, as if the authority or body were an enforcement agency.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-50-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd26fa278db01b5ac3bb0f403b755969282cffd2431d1eff5775f6a3c381d319",
      "skos:note": "Continuation of existing authorisation after commencement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-2-sec-50",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50 Existing authorisations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "If:\n\n(a) an authority or body made an authorisation under Division 4\nof Part 4-1 of the Telecommunications (Interception and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nRestricting access to stored communications and telecommunications data  Schedule 2\nApplication provisions  Part 3\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\nAccess) Act 1979 before the commencement of this Schedule;\nand\n\n(b) the authorisation was in force immediately before that\ncommencement; and\n\n(c) on that commencement, the authority or body is not an\nenforcement agency;\nafter that commencement, the authorisation continues in force, and\nChapter 4 of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979 as amended by this Act continues to apply in relation to the\nauthorisation, as if the authority or body were an enforcement agency."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-50-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-50"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-51",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51 Evidentiary certificates",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-2-sec-51"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf:\n\n(a) an authority or body issued a certificate under section 107U\nor 130 of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access)\nAct 1979 before the commencement of this Schedule; and\n\n(b) on that commencement, the authority or body is not a\ncriminal law-enforcement agency (whether or not it is an\nenforcement agency);\nafter that commencement, the certificate continues in force as if the\nauthority or body were a criminal law-enforcement agency.\n(2)\nIf:\n\n(a) an authority or body issued a certificate under section 185C\nof the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979 before the commencement of this Schedule; and\n\n(b) on that commencement, the authority or body is not an\nenforcement agency;\nafter that commencement, the certificate continues in force as if the\nauthority or body were an enforcement agency.\n(3)\nAn authority or body that:\n\n(a) was a criminal law-enforcement agency immediately before\nthe commencement of this Schedule; and\n\n(b) on that commencement, is not a criminal law-enforcement\nagency (whether or not it is an enforcement agency);\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 2  Restricting access to stored communications and telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf:\n\n(a) an authority or body issued a certificate under section 107U\nor 130 of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access)\nAct 1979 before the commencement of this Schedule; and\n\n(b) on that commencement, the authority or body is not a\ncriminal law-enforcement agency (whether or not it is an\nenforcement agency);\nafter that commencement, the certificate continues in force as if the\nauthority or body were a criminal law-enforcement agency.\n(2)\nIf:\n\n(a) an authority or body issued a certificate under section 185C\nof the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979 before the commencement of this Schedule; and\n\n(b) on that commencement, the authority or body is not an\nenforcement agency;\nafter that commencement, the certificate continues in force as if the\nauthority or body were an enforcement agency.\n(3)\nAn authority or body that:\n\n(a) was a criminal law-enforcement agency immediately before\nthe commencement of this Schedule; and\n\n(b) on that commencement, is not a criminal law-enforcement\nagency (whether or not it is an enforcement agency);\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 2  Restricting access to stored communications and telecommunications data",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-51-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-51-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-51-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-51-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-51-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-2-sec-51-logic-alleninterval-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "780e9c9a052c72b0efd804a75040406cf361a857821624005b9504378f9db2dc",
      "skos:note": "Certificates issued under certain sections of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 continue in force after commencement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-2-sec-51",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51 Evidentiary certificates",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf:\n\n(a) an authority or body issued a certificate under section 107U\nor 130 of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access)\nAct 1979 before the commencement of this Schedule; and\n\n(b) on that commencement, the authority or body is not a\ncriminal law-enforcement agency (whether or not it is an\nenforcement agency);\nafter that commencement, the certificate continues in force as if the\nauthority or body were a criminal law-enforcement agency.\n(2)\nIf:\n\n(a) an authority or body issued a certificate under section 185C\nof the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979 before the commencement of this Schedule; and\n\n(b) on that commencement, the authority or body is not an\nenforcement agency;\nafter that commencement, the certificate continues in force as if the\nauthority or body were an enforcement agency.\n(3)\nAn authority or body that:\n\n(a) was a criminal law-enforcement agency immediately before\nthe commencement of this Schedule; and\n\n(b) on that commencement, is not a criminal law-enforcement\nagency (whether or not it is an enforcement agency);\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 2  Restricting access to stored communications and telecommunications data"
    },
    {
