      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.83",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Ombudsman has reasonable grounds to believe that an\nofficer of a particular enforcement agency is able to give\ninformation relevant to an inspection under this Chapter of the\nagency’s records, the Ombudsman may:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 3  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Ombudsman has reasonable grounds to believe that an\nofficer of a particular enforcement agency is able to give\ninformation relevant to an inspection under this Chapter of the\nagency’s records, the Ombudsman may:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nSchedule 3  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman",
      "cml:asserts": [
