    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "186F Exchange of information between Ombudsman and State",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-3-sec-186f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "inspecting authorities\n\n(1) If the Ombudsman has obtained under this Act information relating\nto an authority of a State or Territory, the Ombudsman may give\nthe information to another authority of that State or Territory (an\ninspecting authority) that:\n\n(a) has powers under the law of that State or Territory; and\n\n(b) has the function of making inspections of a similar kind to\nthose provided for in section 186B of this Act when the\ninspecting authority is exercising those powers.\n\n(2) However, the Ombudsman may give the information only if the\nOmbudsman is satisfied that giving the information is necessary to\nenable the inspecting authority to perform its functions in relation\nto the authority of the State or Territory.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may receive, from an inspecting authority,\ninformation relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions under this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "inspecting authorities\n\n(1) If the Ombudsman has obtained under this Act information relating\nto an authority of a State or Territory, the Ombudsman may give\nthe information to another authority of that State or Territory (an\ninspecting authority) that:\n\n(a) has powers under the law of that State or Territory; and\n\n(b) has the function of making inspections of a similar kind to\nthose provided for in section 186B of this Act when the\ninspecting authority is exercising those powers.\n\n(2) However, the Ombudsman may give the information only if the\nOmbudsman is satisfied that giving the information is necessary to\nenable the inspecting authority to perform its functions in relation\nto the authority of the State or Territory.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may receive, from an inspecting authority,\ninformation relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions under this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186f-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "516548d0cfde581deae940307cc8454dbb916b4cc2940cc91b4c9f8de1a1586b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-3-sec-186f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "186F Exchange of information between Ombudsman and State",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "inspecting authorities\n\n(1) If the Ombudsman has obtained under this Act information relating\nto an authority of a State or Territory, the Ombudsman may give\nthe information to another authority of that State or Territory (an\ninspecting authority) that:\n\n(a) has powers under the law of that State or Territory; and\n\n(b) has the function of making inspections of a similar kind to\nthose provided for in section 186B of this Act when the\ninspecting authority is exercising those powers.\n\n(2) However, the Ombudsman may give the information only if the\nOmbudsman is satisfied that giving the information is necessary to\nenable the inspecting authority to perform its functions in relation\nto the authority of the State or Territory.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may receive, from an inspecting authority,\ninformation relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions under this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186f-ss-1",
