    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "186G Delegation by Ombudsman",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-3-sec-186g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman may delegate:\n\n(a) to an APS employee responsible to the Ombudsman; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nOversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\n(b) to a person having similar oversight functions to the\nOmbudsman under the law of a State or Territory or to an\nemployee responsible to that person;\nall or any of the Ombudsman’s powers under this Chapter other\nthan a power to report to the Minister.\n\n(2) A delegate must, upon request by a person affected by the exercise\nof any power delegated to the delegate, produce the instrument of\ndelegation, or a copy of the instrument, for inspection by the\nperson.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Ombudsman may delegate:\n\n(a) to an APS employee responsible to the Ombudsman; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nOversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\n(b) to a person having similar oversight functions to the\nOmbudsman under the law of a State or Territory or to an\nemployee responsible to that person;\nall or any of the Ombudsman’s powers under this Chapter other\nthan a power to report to the Minister.\n\n(2) A delegate must, upon request by a person affected by the exercise\nof any power delegated to the delegate, produce the instrument of\ndelegation, or a copy of the instrument, for inspection by the\nperson.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186g-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "97afd8c63eddcbfb4b8541e452c77e1babb9cfd285a815cec001a0702e1ef4ef"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015#sch-3-sec-186g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "186G Delegation by Ombudsman",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman may delegate:\n\n(a) to an APS employee responsible to the Ombudsman; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039\n\nOversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 39, 2015\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data\nRetention) Act 2015\n\n(b) to a person having similar oversight functions to the\nOmbudsman under the law of a State or Territory or to an\nemployee responsible to that person;\nall or any of the Ombudsman’s powers under this Chapter other\nthan a power to report to the Minister.\n\n(2) A delegate must, upon request by a person affected by the exercise\nof any power delegated to the delegate, produce the instrument of\ndelegation, or a copy of the instrument, for inspection by the\nperson."
    },
